  m_Name: case_8
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CaseData
  id: 8
  context: "THE UNEASE OF THE CRITIC AT THE BISTRO DES HALLES\nSunday evening, at
    9:20 p.m., the gastronomic critic Jean-Marc Delaunay collapsed at table 7 of
    the Bistrot des Halles. The analyses reveal a powerful sleeping pill in his glass
    of red wine (a Saint-\xC9milion). The previous month, he had published a murderous
    review of the restaurant. Ten people were able to approach his glass between
    8:50 p.m. and 9:15 p.m."
  facts: "Bottle opened at table 7 at 8:50 p.m., glass filled at 8:52 p.m. \nA non-staff
    person entered the kitchen at 8:58 p.m. \nDessert (tarte tatin) Was served at
    9:10 p.m. \nWhite powder found on the briefcase and the room camera did not record
    the phone \nOne waiter in a black apron was seen leaning over table 7"
  suspects:
